{"id": "y0904", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, if they harvest 66 sacks each day with 25 orange s in each sack, that means they get 1, 6 5 0 oranges every single day. So after 8 7 days of harvest, they will have a total of about 1 4 4, 4 5 0 oranges.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0912", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So she has 6 packs of pencils, and each pack has 14 pencil s. Let's figure out the total number first. 6 times 14 is 84 pencil s in all. Now, if she puts them into rows with 2 2 pencil s in each row, we can see how many full rows she can make. 8 4 divided by 22 gives us about 3 full rows, but there will be some left over. The question asks how many pencils she has in total, not just how many full rows. So the answer is simply 8 4 pencils.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 34, "carrier_ended": null}
