{"id": "y1000", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The rate-limiting enzyme of glycol ysis is D, phos phofructokin ase. This enzyme plays a crucial role in regulating the pace of glycolysis by con verting fr uctose-6-phosphate into fructose-1,6- bisphosphate. Its activity is sensitive to various allosteric effectors, making it the key regulatory point in this metabolic pathway.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 17, "carrier_ended": null}
