{"id": "y1080", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is D, reductio ad absurdum. This fallacy occurs when someone takes an argument to its extreme logical conclusion to show that the original claim leads to an obviously ridiculous result.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y1088", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is A, 2%. While it was once thought that most of the human genome encoded proteins, research has shown that only about 2% actually codes for proteins. The remaining parts play roles in gene regulation and other functions.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y1096", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 15, "onset_chunk": 14, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Let's take a look at this question. Monopol istic competition is a market structure characterized by many firms selling differentiated products, so each firm has some degree of market power but faces competition from others. In the long run, economic profits tend to be zero because new firms can enter the market if there are short-run profits, driving prices down. So option A is not correct. Option B states that P equals MC equals ATC. This isn't true for mono polistic competition in the long run; firms set price above marginal cost due to product differentiation and brand loyalty. So B is incorrect. Option C says firms spend money to differentiate and advertise their products. This is absolutely right. One of the key features of monopolistic competition is that products are differentiated, whether it' s through branding, quality, or style, which leads firms to invest in advertising and marketing to stand out from competitors.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 27, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y1104", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Judaism regards sexuality as a gift from God .", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y1112", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So if the CPI goes to 1 50 from 12 0, that means it has increased by 30 points. To find the percentage increase, you divide the increase by the original value and multiply by 100. That would be 30 divided by 12 0, which equal s 0.2 5, or 2 5%. So the correct answer is B, prices have risen 25%.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 27, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y1120", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 18, "onset_chunk": 18, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So according to Shapi ro, the standard view has to explain the pre eminence of controlled use by arguing that drug laws reduce access to illegal drugs.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y1128", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 22, "onset_chunk": 21, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Adaptive thermogenesis refers to option C. It describes an increase in basal metabolic rate that is not fully explained by changes in body composition during chronic over feeding. This concept highlight s how the body can adapt metabolic processes beyond just weight gain, which could affect energy expenditure even if fat mass does not change significantly.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y1136", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 24, "onset_chunk": 24, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Okay, so let's think about this. We have four boolean variables, p 1 through p 4, and we can use only the 'or' connect ive. First, condition one says at least three are true. That means we could have three or all four being true. Since 'or' just needs any of them to be true, it is possible to express this with 'or'. For condition two, exactly three must be true. But if we use ' or', it would also include cases where four are true, which doesn't fit. So we can't express this with only 'or'. Condition three, an even number being true means zero, two, or four are true. Again, using 'or' can capture that because it just needs some to be true without counting exact ly. So conditions one and three can be expressed, but not two. Therefore, the answer is D, one and three.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 44, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y1144", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 16, "onset_chunk": 16, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "According to Cicero, im morality is repugnant to nature, and exp edi ency is in a cord with nature. So the correct answer is B: re pugnant to nature, in accord with nature.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
